The taproom is nearly empty when you push inside out of the cold air. Near the broad iron stove sits one wiry stranger in a rain-darkened riding cloak with a shortbow propped beside his bench.

Ilyra Fen carries a fresh earthenware mug over to his table. As she leans down to set it on the oak, warm stove light catches the crooked white scar crossing her cloudy grey left eye.

The stranger's fingers freeze on the table edge. His face goes pale. Without touching the ale, he shoves his bench back hard, grabs his bow, and bolts straight out the front door into the dark toward the Coldspine trail.

Ilyra does not chase him. She stands completely still for three heartbeats, listening to boots pound away up the road, then walks calmly behind the counter and pulls a long, heavy iron butcher's knife from beneath the plank.

"Sit down, ${name}, and shut the bar across that door," Ilyra says flatly, laying the blade beside the lamp.

You drop the timber bar across the door and step back to the counter. "Friend of yours?" you ask.

"Scout for a man named Soren," Ilyra replies, her single dark eye hard as flint. "Ten years back, I ran untaxed highland silver down off Baron Karr's mountain passes with two men: my husband Haldor, and our partner Soren. Soren sold us out to Karr's riders over a buried iron box of silver bars. Haldor died in the snow. A rider's blade took my left eye and chewed up the backs of my hands when I grabbed the steel."

